# L §8.3 item 9 (round 19, GD-4): "A move's day and a leg's place are seen where they are written as literals or keys of
# a declared index, and where they are computed from these alone, folded through built-ins that read no fact (`on
# end_of(m)` for a key m of a declared index is seen); a day or place computed from a row's value is not seen". L §5.14.1:
# a decision's plain bal(x, d) on its own day or after it is refused, "LOAD-CYCLE where load sees the day (§8.3),
# otherwise RUN-CYCLE on the decision's day and RUN-FUTURE after it".
# on day_of(m, dom), dom a row: load doesn't see the day, so the read of bal(konto, end_of(m)) after it is RUN-FUTURE at
# the read.
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
input floor: money PLN
input dom: int

move save[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto, end_of(m)) - floor)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  floor = 100.00 PLN "own"
  dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask s1: bal(savings, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
s1: refused: RUN-FUTURE a decision on 2026-01-05 reads konto at 2026-02-01 after its day
  cut 2026-01-01
